  "seeded": "paper, Revolut X, BTC/USD + ETH/USD, entryBps 15 on the touch basis - a measurement first, a trade only when the touch itself dislocates",
  "caveat": "The study measured 1-minute CLOSES. A check of the same data (m1/stale_check.py) found 60-73 % of the 'cheap' Revolut X minutes had ZERO Revolut X volume - a carried last-trade print, not a quote - and that the REFERENCE's own forward return after a cheap print is about zero (BTC k=15: -1.9 / +4.1 / +1.9 bps at 5 / 15 / 30 min; ETH: +0.8 / +0.2 / +5.3) while the Revolut X close 'recovers' +20-30 bps. The measured edge is therefore the stale print catching up, which a live order at the touch cannot capture. The rule as shipped reads the TOUCH basis (both venues' live mids), the tradable quantity; the loop's own observations and agent_basis will show how often the touch itself sits 15 bps under Kraken. Until that record exists the numbers here are an upper bound, not an expectation.",
